    "title": "pandas.Series.cat.as_ordered — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1661.gf74cda2e6e documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.cat.as_ordered#\n\n- Series.cat.as_ordered()[source]#\n- Set the Categorical to be ordered. This method returns a new Categorical with the ordered attribute set to True, enabling comparison operations between categories. \n  - Returns:\n    - Categorical\n    - Ordered Categorical.\n See also \n  - `as_unordered`\n  - Set the Categorical to be unordered.\n Examples For `pandas.Series` :>>> ser = pd.Series([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"a\"], dtype=\"category\") >>> ser.cat.ordered False >>> ser = ser.cat.as_ordered() >>> ser.cat.ordered True For `pandas.CategoricalIndex` :>>> ci = pd.CategoricalIndex([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"a\"]) >>> ci.ordered False >>> ci = ci.as_ordered() >>> ci.ordered True",
    "markdown_length": 684,
